  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 257 PM EDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\n===== Friday through the Weekend =====\n\nThe upper ridge will continue to dominate the central US on Friday, \nbut will begin to see signs of it building back to the west as two \nupper lows on the opposite ends of the country squeeze and amplify \nthe ridge. By the weekend, the upper pattern will look somewhat like \nan omega block pattern, but that will only be for a brief time. \n\nSPC has a Day 3 marginal risk across our area for Friday, but \nconfidence in severe weaker risk remains quite low. We'll see a \nslight increase in moisture ahead of an approaching backdoor cold \nfront Friday afternoon, and with strong heating still in place, \nwe'll likely end up seeing steeper lapse rates and favorable \ndestabilization. Isolated thunderstorms could develop, though any \nprecip would likely be rather sparse and brief in nature due to very \nweak shear profiles. Overall, not entirely impressed with the \nmarginal risk, but added an isolated chance for some in the forecast \nfor Friday. The heat Advisory continues through Friday as temps in \nthe upper 90s are expected. \n\nDaily max temps in the 90s are expected through the weekend as we \nremain on the eastern periphery of the ridge. However, the \naforementioned backdoor cold front appears to pass through the area \non Saturday, and should offer additional isolated to scattered \nshowers and storms through the day. We'll still be dealing with \nstrong destabilization due to the heating, however overall shear \nprofiles remain rather weak and less favorable for organized storms. \n\n===== Labor Day and into Next Week =====\n\nDry weather is expected for Labor Day and into the first half of \nnext week as the upper ridge begins to shift east with time again. \nTemps are forecast to be in the lower 90s next week with dewpoints \nin the upper 60s.",
